{"id":"NCT07753993","title":"A Study to Investigate Outcomes With Elecoglipron Compared With Placebo in Adult Participants With Chronic Kidney Disease.","official":"A Phase III, Randomized, Double-blind, Parallel-group, Placebo-controlled Multicenter Study to Evaluate the Effect of Elecoglipron in Reducing Renal Outcomes and Mortality in Participants With Chronic Kidney Disease (Elevate-CKD)","summary":"This is a Phase III, randomized, double-blind, parallel-group, placebo-controlled multicenter study to investigate outcomes with elecoglipron compared with placebo in participants with CKD with and without T2DM who are on background SGLT2i (dapagliflozin) as GDMT and other SoC treatments for CKD.","conditions":["Chronic Kidney Disease"],"interventions":[{"type":"DRUG","name":"Elecoglipron"},{"type":"DRUG","name":"Placebo"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n* Adults with confirmed CKD; UACR ≥30 mg/g and eGFR ≥20 mL/min/1.73 m² within specified ranges.\n* On stable, patient maximum tolerated, labeled daily dose of ACEI or ARB for ≥4 weeks at least 28 days before screening.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n* BMI \\<23 kg/m² at screening\n* History of type 1 diabetes mellitus\n* HbA1c ≥10% (86 mmol/mol) at screening\n* Currently receiving, or anticipated to receive, therapeutic intervention for diabetic retinopathy and/or macular edema.\n* Have had more than one episode of severe hypoglycemia within 180 days prior to screening, or hypoglycemia unawareness\n* Acute coronary syndrome, major cardiac procedure, stroke, or TIA within 3 months prior to screening\n* Clinically significant condition affecting the upper GI tract or chronic use of any medication that affects gastric motility or gastric emptying\n* History of acute or chronic pancreatitis\n* History/family history (first degree) of medullary thyroid cancer or MEN2","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"TREATMENT","enrollment":7000,"start":"2026-08-21","pcd":"2030-10-04","upd":"2026-09-09","sponsor":"AstraZeneca","areas":["other"],"central":["AstraZeneca Clinical Study Information Center · 1-877-240-9479 · information.center@astrazeneca.com"],"sites":[{"f":"Research Site","city":"Huntsville","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35801","s":"NYR","lat":34.7304,"lon":-86.5859,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Montgomery","pr":"Alabama","zip":"36117","s":"NYR","lat":32.3668,"lon":-86.3,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Sheffield","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35660","s":"NYR","lat":34.7651,"lon":-87.6986,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Peoria","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85382","s":"NYR","lat":33.5806,"lon":-112.2374,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Phoenix","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85012","s":"NYR","lat":33.4484,"lon":-112.074,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Surprise","pr":"Arizona","zip":"85374","s":"NYR","lat":33.6306,"lon":-112.3332,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"STOP","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Chula Vista","pr":"California","zip":"91910","s":"NYR","lat":32.6401,"lon":-117.0842,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Concord","pr":"California","zip":"94520","s":"NYR","lat":37.978,"lon":-122.0311,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Daly City","pr":"California","zip":"94015","s":"NYR","lat":37.7058,"lon":-122.4619,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Fremont","pr":"California","zip":"94538","s":"NYR","lat":37.5483,"lon":-121.9886,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Huntington Beach","pr":"California","zip":"92647","s":"NYR","lat":33.6603,"lon":-117.9992,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Huntington Park","pr":"California","zip":"90255","s":"NYR","lat":33.9817,"lon":-118.2251,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"Lomita","pr":"California","zip":"90717","s":"NYR","lat":33.7922,"lon":-118.3151,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","city":"National City","pr":"California","zip":"91950","s":"NYR","lat":32.6781,"lon":-117.0992,"c":""},{"f":"Research Site","